# ~/.config/wl-cast/buttons: the stream page's own buttons, in order.
# One per line: a label, then the command it runs on the host.  The command
# runs through Sway, on the stream's screen, with WL_CAST_OUTPUT (that
# screen) and WL_CAST_PANEL (the one streamed) set.  Changes show at the
# page's next reload.  Three fingers tapped on the page fold or show the
# buttons; held, they show them on a wheel.
#
# They sit at the bottom left, after the built-in CTRL, SUPER, ALT, LKB and the arrow.
# A line [top-right] puts the buttons after it at the top right, beside the
# page's own, and [bottom-left] back; =lkb, =place, =super, =ctrl and =alt place
# the built-in ones where they appear.
#
# On the wheel (three fingers held), your buttons share one sector, APPS,
# unless a line [group NAME] gives the ones after it a sector NAME of their
# own (until the next [group] line; [group] alone goes back to APPS).  The
# groups come in the order the file names them, before the page's own.
#
# The commands below are placeholders: put your own launcher, window
# switcher, menu or on-screen keyboard there.
OSK   notify-send wl-cast "OSK: your on-screen keyboard here"
WIN   notify-send wl-cast "WIN: your window switcher here"
QA    notify-send wl-cast "QA: your quick settings here"
APPS  notify-send wl-cast "APPS: your app launcher here"
# e.g. a second sector on the wheel:
#[group MEDIA]
#PLAY  playerctl play-pause
#NEXT  playerctl next
